  <name>Melograph</name>
  <summary>Turn piano recordings into sheet music</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="de">Klavieraufnahmen in Noten verwandeln</summary>
  <developer id="net.devemperor">
    <name>DevEmperor</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Melograph listens to a piano recording and writes it down as engraved sheet music:
      both hands on a grand staff, with metre, key, pedal, slurs, dynamics and ornaments.
      The result opens in MuseScore or is exported as MusicXML, PDF, MIDI or MEI.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Note recognition with Transkun, beats and bars with Beat This!</li>
      <li>Hand split, voices, triplets, swing, grace notes, trills and rolled chords</li>
      <li>Pedal marks, phrase slurs, hairpins, accents, fermatas, 8va lines and clef changes</li>
      <li>Live score preview that follows the recording, side by side with a piano roll</li>
      <li>Everything runs on your own computer, no account and no upload</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">net.devemperor.Melograph.desktop</launchable>
